GNOME Power Manager 2.32 on logind and UPower 0.99 (VoltOS).

- egg-console-kit.c talks to logind instead of ConsoleKit: the session
  (active, remote) is the caller's logind session, whose Active property
  changes stand in for ConsoleKit's ActiveChanged; stop and restart are
  logind's PowerOff and Reboot.  It also suspends and hibernates (logind's
  Suspend and Hibernate, waiting for PrepareForSleep(false) so that, as
  with UPower's old synchronous calls, they return after waking up), and
  tells whether the machine can (CanSuspend, CanHibernate): UPower no
  longer does either.
- UpClient's "changed" signal is gone: on-battery and lid-is-closed
  property notifications call the same handlers.
- UpClient's "device-changed" is gone: each device's own notifications
  do; "device-removed" now gives the device's object path.
- up_client_enumerate_devices_sync is gone (the device list is always
  there), and so is the processor wakeup statistics API (UpWakeups):
  up-wakeups-compat.h reports it missing, so the statistics window leaves
  out its Processor page.
- libnotify 0.7: notify_notification_new takes three arguments and no
  longer points at a status icon.

